  "body": "# Associated User Story\n\nAs an officer/manager creating an event, I should not be able to set the end time before the start time at all, as all end time possible times should be starting after the start time.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Officers and managers cannot set an event’s end time before its start time, and only valid end times can be chosen.\n\n**Sunny:** An officer or manager creates or edits an event and picks a start date and time. The end time options then only include times after the start time, so an earlier end time cannot be selected. They choose a valid end time and save, and the event is created with the start and end times shown on the event details page. If they later move the start time to after the current end time, the end time is cleared or adjusted and they are asked to pick a new valid one before saving.\n\n**Rainy:** The officer or manager tries to get around the restriction, for example by typing an end time earlier than or equal to the start time, or by submitting the form manually with an invalid end time. They see a clear message next to the field, such as “End time must be after the start time,” instead of a blank page or a silent failure. The event is not saved until the end time is fixed, and any previously saved times stay unchanged. A regular member who tries to create or edit an event is blocked (officers and managers only).\n\n# Definition of Done\n\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
